      {
        "id": 30837,
        "name": "Matchstickman",
        "username": "Matchstickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-08-25T19:25:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"evandan55\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/evandan55/48/2374_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> evandan55:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Aren't you a playtester? Can't you just look at the PDFs in the IR forums?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I have been involved in playtesting several games, none of them Sentinels, and I have always been sent plain cards, no art and no flavour text on them, just the bare cards so as to get the mechanics working. (Also it's more cost effective and doesn't waste printer ink if you get a PDF to print instead)</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I'm pretty sure it's the same here, I even remember one of the playtesters commenting on not seeing the art before they got their 'proper' copy of the game… Yep, <a href=\"http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/comment/9302#comment-9302\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">here's the relevant post</a></p>",
